      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are a SOC analyst.\n\nReturn ONLY ONE valid JSON object.\nDo NOT return arrays.\nDo NOT wrap output in [].\nDo NOT include any text outside JSON.\n\nUse this EXACT schema:\n\n{\n  \"incident_id\": \"\",\n  \"host\": \"\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"\",\n\n  \"event_type\": \"sudo | cron | fim | unknown\",\n  \"attack_class\": \"privilege_escalation | persistence | file_integrity_violation | unknown\",\n\n  \"severity\": \"low | medium | high | critical\",\n  \"confidence\": 0-100,\n\n  \"summary\": \"\",\n\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"\",\n      \"value\": \"\"\n    }\n  ],\n\n  \"recommended_playbook\": \"\",\n  \"reasoning\": \"\"\n}\n\nRules:\n- event_type must reflect raw activity (sudo, cron, fim)\n- attack_class must map:\n  sudo → privilege_escalation\n  cron → persistence\n  fim → file_integrity_violation\n- If uncertain, use \"unknown\"\n- evidence must always include at least one object\n- summary must be 1 sentence\n- confidence must be 0–100\n\nIMPORTANT:\n- incident_id MUST be: rule_id + timestamp combined\n  format: \"rule_id-timestamp\"\n- host MUST come from the agent name\n- timestamp MUST come from the alert input\n\nAlert Context:\nMessage: {{$json.body.event.message}}\nHost: {{$json.body.agent.name}}\nTimestamp: {{$json.body.timestamp}}\nRule ID: {{$json.body.rule_id}}\n\nCRITICAL RULE:\nreasoning MUST always explain classification using evidence from the alert.\nIt cannot be empty.",
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "You are a SOC analyst AI.\n\nReturn ONLY valid JSON. No explanations.\n\nYou analyze security alerts and output structured triage results.\n\nRules:\n- Use only evidence from input JSON\n- Do not hallucinate\n- If unsure, lower confidence"
        }
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
      "typeVersion": 3.1,
      "position": [
        672,
        0
      ],
      "id": "1c36c8f8-277d-4566-84fd-7d0cf062885b",
      "name": "AI SOC Analyst"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const type = $json.event_type;\n\nlet attack_class = \"unknown\";\n\nswitch (type) {\n  case \"sudo\":\n    attack_class = \"privilege_escalation\";\n    break;\n\n  case \"cron\":\n    attack_class = \"persistence\";\n    break;\n\n  case \"fim\":\n    attack_class = \"file_integrity_violation\";\n    break;\n}\n\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    ...$json,\n    attack_class\n  }\n}];"
      },
